{
  "esm": "0.8.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "ppm_lev_edge",
    "description": "Colella-Woodward (1984) eq. (1.6) non-uniform 4th-order interpolation of a cell-averaged field to the interface a_{j+1/2} between cells j and j+1, on an arbitrarily-spaced 1-D mesh, using the RAW (unlimited) eq. (1.7) average slopes. A thin wrapper: it supplies ../stencils/ppm_lev_slope at cells j and j+1 to the shared eq (1.6) combination ../stencils/ppm_lev_edge_core (which owns the algebra; the monotone sibling ../stencils/ppm_lev_edge_mono is the same wrapper with monotonized slopes, so the eq (1.6) body is written once). Given four consecutive cell averages (am,a0,ap,app) = (a_{j-1},a_j,a_{j+1},a_{j+2}) and their widths (dm,d0,dp,dpp) it returns a_{j+1/2}. On a uniform mesh this collapses exactly to the (7/12)(a0+ap) - (1/12)(am+app) edge of ppm_face_value, and on the quadratic-stretch vertical it is verified 4th-order accurate (interior). UNLIMITED: the raw slopes make this the maximally accurate reconstruction but it is NOT bounded -- the edge value can overshoot the range of the two cells it separates, which on a sharp vertical gradient (a plume, an inversion, the tropopause) produces new extrema and NEGATIVE tracer concentrations. Use the monotone chain (ppm_lev_edge_mono -> ppm_lev_flux_mono -> rules/ppm_D_lev_mono_noflux_bc) for production tracer transport, and this one where the field is smooth and the 4th order is wanted. Grid-agnostic scalar algebra; match-less named template; composed by ppm_lev_flux.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:stencil",
      "family:finite_volume",
      "grid:latlon3d",
      "op:reconstruct",
      "order:4",
      "stencil_width:4"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Colella, P., & Woodward, P. R. (1984). The Piecewise Parabolic Method (PPM) for gas-dynamical simulations. Journal of Computational Physics, 54(1), 174-201. Equations (1.6)-(1.7), non-uniform mesh.",
        "doi": "10.1016/0021-9991(84)90143-8"
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [
    {
      "ref": "./ppm_lev_slope.esm"
    },
    {
      "ref": "./ppm_lev_edge_core.esm"
    }
  ],
  "expression_templates": {
    "ppm_lev_edge": {
      "params": [
        "am",
        "a0",
        "ap",
        "app",
        "dm",
        "d0",
        "dp",
        "dpp"
      ],
      "description": "CW84 eq.(1.6) non-uniform edge a_{j+1/2} using raw eq.(1.7) slopes",
      "body": {
        "op": "apply_expression_template",
        "args": [],
        "name": "ppm_lev_edge_core",
        "bindings": {
          "a0": "a0",
          "ap": "ap",
          "dm": "dm",
          "d0": "d0",
          "dp": "dp",
          "dpp": "dpp",
          "sj": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "ppm_lev_slope",
            "bindings": {
              "am": "am",
              "a0": "a0",
              "ap": "ap",
              "dm": "dm",
              "d0": "d0",
              "dp": "dp"
            }
          },
          "sjp1": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "ppm_lev_slope",
            "bindings": {
              "am": "a0",
              "a0": "ap",
              "ap": "app",
              "dm": "d0",
              "d0": "dp",
              "dp": "dpp"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
